{
  "_comment": "Base weapons are the game's own weapons; ids are what the adapter reports as weapon_id. Affix roll ranges are scaled by economy.json weapon_rarity.magnitude_mult. Units: *_pct percent, crit_chance fraction, supplies_on_kill supplies per kill (fractions add up kill by kill). Elements (2026-11-11, the user: the best tiers carried too many): a gun has one. A gun found or bought at Epic or above rolls it by weight (the better ones less often); a gun refined to Epic offers two by weight and a random one, any as likely, to choose from; at Legendary it evolves (its 'evolved' numbers). An Exotic gun adds one legendary effect (unique_affixes). stream_seconds is the flamethrower's (an enemy in its flame): Shock arcs from it every that many seconds, Cryo freezes it after that many. The flamethrower's Incendiary burns at stream_dps_fraction of its flame's damage a second until stream_total_fraction of it is dealt; its Toxic adds a stack of stream_dps_fraction a second at most every stream_stack_seconds (up to stream_max_stacks), ticking once a second until the enemy dies. Radii are engine units (centimetres); dps_fraction and an arc's damage_fraction are fractions of the hit's damage, a blast's damage_fraction and a cloud's cloud_dps_fraction of the victim's maximum health. Against a boss an element only adds boss_bonus damage (Incendiary and Toxic burn and poison it instead). per_level: what each level above 1 adds to a gun the game gives no levels (amounts a level; WeaponLevelPerks in weapons.h says each).",
